    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13005" root="دلهم" body-key="d">
    
      Q. 4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِدْلَهَمَّ</span></b>  <i>It</i> (the night) <i>was,</i> or <i>became,
black;</i> (TA;) or <i>intensely dark:</i> (Mgh:) and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِدْلَأَمَّ</span> signifies the same; (K and TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دلم</span>;)
the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ء</span> being a substitute for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ه</span>. (TA in that art.)
And <i>It</i> (darkness) <i>was,</i> or <i>became, dense,</i> or <i>thick.</i>
(K.) See the next paragraph. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also <i>He</i> (a man)
<i>was,</i> or <i>became, aged;</i> and so <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِدْلَهَنَّ</span>. (K in
art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دلهن</span>.)

